From: Daniel Pawlik <pawlik.dan@gmail.com>
Subject: net: airoha: npu: fix missing streaming DMA mask

The driver calls dma_set_coherent_mask() but never dma_set_mask(),
leaving the streaming DMA mask at its default. On the non-coherent
EN7581 platform this causes the NPU to hang after approximately 41
mailbox calls.

Replace dma_set_coherent_mask() with dma_set_mask_and_coherent() to
set both masks, matching standard driver practice.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Pawlik <pawlik.dan@gmail.com>

---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c
@@ -769,7 +769,7 @@ static int airoha_npu_probe(struct platf
 		npu->irqs[i] = irq;
 	}
 
-	err = dma_set_coherent_mask(dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(32));
+	err = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(32));
 	if (err)
 		return err;
